# BT Business — Paper Register, Not Tally

## Target user
A shopkeeper who **writes everything in a notebook** today: pan shop, tea stall, kirana, hardware, mobile shop, dairy, bakery, small wholesaler.

**Zero accounting knowledge.** Must be **easier than Tally**.

## Golden rule
If a feature feels like **Tally or accounting software**, remove it or hide it from the user.
The app must always feel like **writing in a paper register**.

## Design principles (permanent)

1. **2–3 taps** — every common task should finish in 2–3 taps when possible.
2. **5–6 fields max** — every form has at most 5–6 fields. Never ask for unnecessary information.
3. **Instant search** — search everywhere by typing a few letters of a name. No IDs, no item codes.
4. **Reports are read-only** — users never edit data from reports/history screens.
5. **History is complete** — never delete old years automatically. Keep unlimited years unless the user manually deletes an entry.
6. **Performance at scale** — stay fast with 100,000+ transactions. Use pagination, lazy loading, and indexed queries.

## UI vocabulary

| Never say | Say instead |
|-----------|-------------|
| Ledger | **Hisaab** |
| Customer / Supplier | **Party** (one party can be both) |
| Inventory tab label | **Items** / **Maal** |
| Sale Invoice / Voucher | **Sale** / **Bikri** |
| Purchase Invoice | **Purchase** / **Kharid** |
| Credit | **Udhaar** |
| Payment received | **Jama** / **Paisa mila** |
| Payment paid | **Paisa diya** |
| Expense | **Kharch** |
| Receivable / Payable | **Lena Hai** / **Dena Hai** |
| Journal, Voucher, Debit, Credit, HSN, GSTIN, Stock Group, Item Code | **Never show in UI** |

Code may use `ledger`, `journal`, `debit` internally — **never expose to users**.

## Item creation (instant — 2 fields only)
- **Item Name** (required)
- **Unit** — Piece, Kg, Gram, Litre, Packet, Box, Meter, Dozen, etc. (required)

Nothing else in the create flow: no category, item code, HSN, GST, opening stock, stock group, purchase/sale price on create.
Stock updates **automatically** after every Sale and Purchase.

## Party creation (instant — up to 3 fields)
- **Name** (required)
- **Mobile** (optional)
- **Previous Balance** (optional — Lena hai / Dena hai)

Nothing else: no GSTIN, credit limit, address, customer/supplier type picker, active/inactive.

## Entry forms (max fields)
- **Jama / Paisa diya**: Party, Amount, Date, Note (optional)
- **Kharch**: Expense Name, Amount, Date, Note (optional)
- **Sale / Purchase**: Party, Date, payment mode, line items (qty + rate) — register style, not invoice

Pick or **instant-create** Party and Item inline from entry screens. No separate master-data detours.

## Automatic (hidden from user)
Stock, hisaab balances, dashboard totals, and history update automatically when entries are saved.
No invoice printing, no bills/PDF/e-way.

## When building new features
- Prefer **simple over powerful** every time.
- Paginate lists; index `date`, `party_id`, `type`, and name search columns.
- History and reports: filter and display only — no inline edit.
